 "about": "The parish church: nave and chancel with aisles and chapels under three parallel roofs, the aisles enveloping the west tower, whose two upper stages are C17 brick. Liturgical east is map north (y 0); the tower is at the map's south end.",
 "evidence": [
  "List entry 1092160 (OGL): the plan (chancel of 2 arcades, nave of 3 and 4 arches, west tower enveloped by the aisles, chapels making a 3-gable east wall), the walling (flint with stone rubble and some brick, 7 stepped buttresses on the long sides), the windows (Decorated and Perpendicular tracery, 2 three-light windows in square frames), the tower (C17 brick, corner pinnacles, crenellated parapet, bell-stage opening in an Ionic frame, stone bands on dentils) and the fittings (C17 pulpit, galleries of 1632, brasses, Royal Arms of 1661, churchwarden's chest, font c.1500).",
  "Build's plan (LiDAR): the box 19 x 35 squares; three ranges 6, 7 and 6 wide, three storeys to the eaves; the tower 7 x 6, six storeys.",
  "Photos looked at, never copied (Commons, CC BY-SA): the west front, the nave and aisles, the pulpit; for colours and proportions only.",
  "Doors: the west door and the north door (0, 15) where the map's paths meet the walls; the south door (19, 20) is the church's south door, which no path on the map reaches: Build's yards.py lays one to it. The buttress at the corner stands at y 33, clear of the path's end (19, 34).",
  "Not built: the buttresses on the north (map west) side - their outside squares are off the building's grid; the tower's thin corner buttresses with Ionic caps; the slight drop of the roof at the east end (the roof is Build's, from the LiDAR); galleries other than the west one. Built as the listing says: the continuous plinth (the plinth trim).",
  "Measured on the west front photo: the tower is flint with stone corner buttresses for its lower third and brick above (brick from storey 2); the aisle windows are about 0.4 of the gable's width, from a third of the wall's height almost to the eaves (two storeys: lights, then head)."
 ],
